cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Gene-Mila: an autonomous, deadline-bounded laboratory for interpretable cell-perturbation prediction"
abstract: >-
  LLM research agents discover features for simple CPU models (ridge, lasso, OLS) that predict how
  gene expression changes under a genetic perturbation the model has never seen. A Python
  controller, never an LLM, owns the deadline, scheduling, spend caps and persistence, and stops
  every agent at the wall-clock budget. Evaluated on CellForge's Adamson and Norman splits.
authors:
